#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""task lifecycle for one task; private evidence lives in ~/.local/state/task.

The sandbox protects private task state from lanes running as the same Unix user.
Write capability there determines trust; vendor environment markers do not.

  task start <repo> <id> --builder codex|claude [--refresh] [--no-verify <reason>] [--seed <name>]...
  task runner-check <repo> <file>
  task runner-start <repo> <runner-file> [--llm]
  task lane <repo> <id> [--model gpt-6-luna|gpt-6.1-sol|gpt-6-astra|sonnet|opus|fable] [--builder codex|claude] [--timeout <minutes>] [--no-boost]
    Claude also accepts claude-sonnet-5-5, claude-opus-5-5, claude-fable-5-1.
    --builder overrides the pinned builder and updates subsequent review routing.
    --seed copies a plain file/directory name from the main checkout's .work/; repeatable.
      Defaults: gpt-6-luna for codex; sonnet for claude.
  task check [[<repo>] <id>] [--detach] [--lock-wait <minutes>]
  task review <repo> <id> [--request <file>] [--append-prompt <text>] [--run | --record <file>] [--no-check <reason>] [--reviewer <vendor> <model>]
  task merge <repo> <id> [--keep] [--override <reason>] [--detach] [--lock-wait <minutes>]
  task cancel <repo> <id>
  task close <repo> <id> -m <summary> --retro <text> [--partial] [--no-merge <reason>]
  task note <repo> <id> improve|intervention|setup <text>
  task note - - setup-done <n>
  task status [<repo>]
  task boost [--claude-until <ISO datetime>] [--codex-until <ISO datetime>]
  task boost off [--claude] [--codex]
  task repair [<repo>]
  task wait <repo> <id> [--max <minutes>]
  task denials [--days N] [--rule R] [--repo R]

<repo> is a folder name in ~/dev_workspace or a path. <id> is a Backlog.md task (T-32, t32, 32)
or a plain name for work without a task. `task start` pins criteria and Verify commands; `task
check` runs the gate and pinned verification; review and merge are PM actions.
Sessions unable to write ~/.local/state/task are advisory lanes. The PM shell and
an unsandboxed batch runner are trusted. Always launch builders via `task lane`;
it keeps the builders sandboxed, including when the runner itself uses bypass.
"""
